# Storybook (frontend component baseline)

When **using**, **composing**, or **handing off** UI from `frontend/components/` (especially `components/ui/`), treat **Storybook** as the canonical reference for how the component looks and which props/variants exist — not ad-hoc copies from pages or guesswork from the source file alone.

## Before reuse

1. Check for a co-located story: `components/**/*.stories.tsx` (same folder as the component).
2. If a story exists, match **variant**, **size**, and usage shown there (light/dark is already wired in `.storybook/preview.tsx` via `ThemeProvider`).
3. If no story exists yet for a piece under `frontend/components/**` you depend on, add a minimal story first (or in the same change) so Storybook stays the baseline.

## Mandatory stories (same change)

| Trigger | Requirement |
|---------|-------------|
| **New** `.tsx` under `frontend/components/**` that exports a **visible** React component | Add co-located `<basename>.stories.tsx` in the **same change** |
| **Edit** props, variants, layout, or behavior stories should reflect | Update existing stories or add a new story variant |
| **`make frontend-shadcn-add`** | Co-located story per [design-system.mdc](design-system.mdc) Base UI |

**Exceptions** (no separate story required):

- Provider-only modules (e.g. `theme-provider.tsx`)
- Null-render app sync helpers (e.g. `ThemeDocumentSync`)
- Hooks exported from component files — cover via the visual component’s story (e.g. `useMounted` via `ThemeModeSwitch` / `LocaleThemeToolbar`)

## Agent workflow (component changes)

Applies when **editing or adding** anything under `frontend/components/**` (`ui/`, `molecules/`, `organisms/`, and shared root components such as `locale-switch.tsx`).

1. Add or update co-located `*.stories.tsx` per **Mandatory stories (same change)** — not optional for new visual exports.
2. Before marking the task done, from repo root run **`make frontend-storybook-build`** — required verification (compile/static build; no dev server required).
3. If the build fails, fix stories, imports, and types in the same turn before completing the task.

Page-only work under `frontend/app/**` that does not touch `components/` does not require this build unless the same change adds or edits shared components or stories.

Atomic reuse and user approval for **new** shared components: [design-system.mdc](design-system.mdc).

## Warehouse pages (`frontend/app/**`)

When **creating or changing** route pages under `frontend/app/` (including `[locale]/…`), treat Storybook as the **implementation spec** for shared UI—not the component source file alone and not copy-pasted `design/` markup.

| Step | Requirement |
|------|-------------|
| **Inventory** | Before writing page JSX, map each UI block to an existing story: sidebar **UI/** and **Molecules/**, plus **Design system/Overview → Catalog** for matrices and cross-cutting chrome. |
| **Compose** | Import **molecules/organisms** (or minimal `ui/` only where stories do). Match **variant**, **size**, **orientation**, and state classes (invalid, success, warning) as shown in stories. |
| **Forms** | Production CRUD/forms: follow [forms.mdc](forms.mdc) via **Molecules/FormField** and related molecule stories (search, status, switches). **UI/Field** stories are primitive layout/state demos only—they do not override form validation rules on pages. |
| **Lists/tables** | Follow [tables.mdc](tables.mdc) using storied molecules (pagination bar, table icon actions, filters)—match story layout and i18n patterns. |
| **Gap** | If the page needs a pattern with no story, add or update `*.stories.tsx` in the same change (see **Before reuse**), then use it on the page. Do not leave one-off route markup as the source of truth. |
| **Verify** | Changes that **only** touch `app/**` do not require `make frontend-storybook-build`. If the same change edits `components/` or stories, run the build as in **Agent workflow (component changes)**. |

## Running Storybook

From repo root: `make frontend-storybook` → [http://localhost:6006](http://localhost:6006) — optional for local visual review; not the required agent checkpoint.

Static catalog / agent verify: `make frontend-storybook-build` → `frontend/storybook-static/`.

Config: `.cursor/skills/frontend/SKILL.md` and `document/knowledge/frontend.md`.

## i18n in stories

Components that call `useTranslations` need `NextIntlClientProvider` + messages in the story decorator — the global preview only covers theme/styles.

## Do not

- Invent one-off styling for shadcn/ui primitives when a story already documents the intended variants.
- Implement route UI by reading component source alone when a matching Storybook story exists.
- Add a new visible component under `frontend/components/**` (`ui/`, `molecules/`, `organisms/`, or shared root chrome) without a co-located story in the same change.
- Skip Storybook when adding a new export that other routes or organisms will import.
- Finish `frontend/components/**` work without running `make frontend-storybook-build` when the change touched that tree.
